From 1622b106295173eaf6059c332ae5197712ef57b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:19:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] Lab: pipelines given back without a driver blob are
 counted and logged when built again

pso_async::code: a pipeline remembers whether its last build left no
driver blob for the next one (the build note of real.rs, or a build
again whose slowest compile took 1 s or more without a blob). The
"shader code lab:" line ends with "given back without a blob N", and
a build again of 1 s or more logs "built again at bind: kind, record,
ms, thread, blob yes/no".

XCL_PSO_KEEP_BLOBLESS=1 (off by default): XCL_PSO_UNUSED_S does not
give back a pipeline without a blob; the XCL_PSO_CODE_MB budget still
may, so any pipeline can still be released to stay under the driver's
code heap.

Tests: the_unused_delay_keeps_a_pipeline_without_a_blob_only_with_the_
switch, a_pipeline_is_without_a_blob_when_its_build_says_so_or_a_slow_
build_again_had_none, a_slow_build_again_is_logged_with_its_compile_
thread_and_blob, a_pipeline_given_back_without_a_blob_is_counted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/xcl/src/hle/d3d12x/pso_async.rs | 157 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 152 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

